comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T13:01:11.067Z","harness:claude-code","Observation 2026-07-27 on the denominator used to compute the failure rate.\n\nThe Auto Release workflow has three triggers and they produce wildly different run volumes. The schedule fires once a day, which is the 84 runs this item measures. The workflow_dispatch fires on demand. The issues trigger fires on every issue closure in the repository, and because there is no concurrency key that collapses them, closing several issues at once produces a burst of near-simultaneous runs: four runs within one second at 12:09:44Z today, six at 08:45 on 2026-07-26, five at 08:54 today with one of them cancelled.\n\nThey are all correctly filtered at job level by the if condition that restricts issues-triggered runs to the bot-authored blocker recovery, so they skip in seconds and cannot cut a release. Two things still follow. The workflow run history is dominated by runs that were never going to do anything, which makes the pipeline look far busier and far healthier than the scheduled path actually is, and any rate computed over all runs rather than over event equals schedule will be wrong by an order of magnitude. And one of today's burst runs shows conclusion cancelled rather than skipped, which is the cancel-in-progress pattern that this project has already learned masks red gates elsewhere.\n\nNeither changes the 32 of 84 scheduled figure this item owns, which was measured on the schedule event alone. Recording it so the denominator is not silently recomputed the easy way later."
  "2026-07-31T06:14:42.055Z","harness:claude-code","Rate sample refreshed 2026-07-31: of the last eleven completed scheduled Auto Release runs, three concluded failure (2026-07-21, 2026-07-23, 2026-07-24) — 27 percent. Consistent with the 32-of-84 lifetime figure. Today's run succeeded and published 2026.7.31; npm latest, npx direct, npx --package and bunx --bun all resolve and execute the published artifact under bun 1.3.11. One scheduled cut today, so the one-release-per-day property held on this run."
  "2026-08-01T09:53:05.449Z","harness:claude-code","Scheduled-run health sampled live 2026-08-01. The most recent scheduled Auto Release runs (30686302858 at 05:41:09Z today, 51s, success; 30607915788 at 2026-07-31T05:50:49Z, 20m50s, success) both completed, and the daily cut is landing: v2026.7.29 through v2026.8.1 exist as consecutive daily tags with matching GitHub releases. The window observation from pm-44u3wt still holds -- the 05:41 and 05:50 start times are hours after the declared cron -- and remains a separate defect from the failure rate this item measures. The point that motivates this item is unchanged and visible in the same listing: the workflow also fires on issues events, and those runs report conclusion 'skipped' while occupying the same run history as real scheduled attempts, so any rate computed over gh run list without partitioning by event conflates three populations (schedule, workflow_dispatch, issues) whose expected outcomes differ."
  "2026-08-03T11:17:38.250Z","harness:codex","Current evidence 2026-08-03: scheduled run 30788639874 succeeded and correctly avoided a second release after v2026.8.3 already existed. This is a healthy point observation, not evidence that the historical reliability-rate gap is resolved; several earlier workflow_dispatch runs on the same day failed before the successful dispatch, so the rolling-rate and cause taxonomy remain necessary."
  "2026-08-04T09:19:16.541Z","harness:codex","Current point evidence 2026-08-04: scheduled Auto Release run 30880997668 succeeded and produced v2026.8.4, followed by successful tag-driven Release run 30881541650. This is a healthy daily observation, not resolution of the historical scheduled-failure-rate problem; issue-triggered skipped runs and prior dispatch failures remain separate populations."
  "2026-08-05T06:17:58.765Z","harness:codex","Scheduled reliability instance 2026-08-05: Auto Release run 30978379616 failed before tag creation in tracker-measurement-gate. Root cause is environment parity: CI runs pm merge install before tracker measurement, while run-release-pipeline did not, so a clean scheduled runner reported five clone-local merge-driver warnings as repository debt. Active remediation is pm-ei6x66; no v2026.8.5 tag, npm package, or GitHub Release existed at diagnosis time."
  "2026-08-07T17:13:33.862Z","harness:claude-code","Rate re-measured live 2026-08-07 over the fourteen most recent scheduled runs: twelve success, two failure, so 85.7 percent on the trigger that carries the daily guarantee. The two failures are 2026-08-05, blocked by static-quality-gate, and 2026-08-07, blocked by sentry-telemetry-gate on \"TypeError: Author acknowledgment target pm-iimv:1 is not an actionable unknown-author event\" at candidate 36360b4b.\n\nThe second one is worth recording precisely because it is not a counterexample to pm-c3uru0's fix. That fix, which routes acknowledgment refusals through PmCliError with EXIT_CODE.USAGE, landed at 3bcacdee on 2026-08-07 07:49, and the failing scheduled run started at 04:36 against a candidate that predates it. The candidate was not red; the fix had simply not landed yet.\n\nWhat the pair does show is the shape this item names. Both failures were repaired by a commit and then released by a manual workflow_dispatch, so the release record shows a successful cut on both days and the scheduled failure survives only in the run list. A reader reconstructing release health from tags, from npm dist-tags, or from the changelog sees fourteen consecutive daily releases. The rate is visible only by listing runs filtered to the schedule event, which is the measurement this item exists to institutionalize."
  "2026-08-08T10:14:59.027Z","harness:codex","2026-08-08 scheduled run 31238168668 failed in sentry-telemetry-gate after all preceding package and release gates passed. Blocking issues were PM-CLI-2S (raw ENOSPC copyfile, three events, last seen 2026-07-30) and PM-CLI-2Q (snapshot-name validation refusal, one event, last seen 2026-07-29). Live Sentry inspection on 2026-08-08 shows both resolved. The active pm-3lhth4 tranche adds stable path-redacted host-fault translation for ENOSPC and other errno classes at the SDK boundary; exact-head preflight and the next release retry remain required before GH #934 can close."
body: ""
